-- member_content_write_gates (quick 261112-kuk; closes Phase 10 gap MPUB-04 and review warnings WR-03, WR-04, WR-05;
-- D-706, D-708, D-713, D-716, D-718; T-kuk-01 to T-kuk-06) — the DATABASE refuses the writes the API alone refused.
--
-- A FILE IN TWO HALVES (the precedent of `20260925191156_story_highlights.sql`). Half 1 is GENERATED by
-- `pnpm db:generate --name=member_content_write_gates` from the policy declarations in
-- `packages/modules/stories/db/schema.ts` and `packages/modules/feed/db/schema.ts`: seven restrictive policies
-- (`stories_member_delete_gate`, the three `story_highlights_member_*_gate`, the three
-- `story_highlight_items_member_*_gate`) and one ALTER POLICY (`feed_posts_social_insert_gate`). Half 2 is HAND-WRITTEN
-- (Drizzle does not model functions or triggers): `app.stories_member_update_guard()` plus its trigger, and the
-- re-created `app.media_asset_hidden`. Neither half calls anything the other defines.
--
-- WHY STORIES UPDATE IS A TRIGGER AND NOT A POLICY. A policy cannot limit columns, and a USING-filtered UPDATE matches
-- zero rows silently. The like and comment counter triggers of a story run as the INVOKER (the member who liked or
-- commented), updating `like_count` / `comment_count` of a story that member did not write; a restrictive UPDATE policy
-- narrowed to the author would turn every such update into a silent zero-row update and the counters would drift. The
-- guard copies `app.feed_posts_member_update_guard` (`20261020123631`, rewritten as an allow-list by `20261111144205`):
-- it holds only a `member` claim, so staff, system lanes and the migration role are untouched.
--   THE RULE for a `member` claim: on a story it did not write only the two counters may change; on ANY story
--   `author_user_id`, `visibility`, `tenant_id` and `media_asset_id` are frozen; on its own story the only columns that
--   may change are the counters and `deleted_at`, and `deleted_at` only as the transition null -> value (the service's
--   soft delete; `stories` has no `deleted_by` column). A violation raises SQLSTATE 42501 with a fixed message that names
--   no row data. Stories have no member hard delete: `stories_member_delete_gate` filters it to zero rows.
--
-- WHY THE ITEM INSERT GATE PINS THE STORY'S AUTHOR (D-716; T-10-34 and T-10-35 mirrored in the database): without it a
-- creator could save ANOTHER member's followers-only story into its own community's highlight, and branch 3 of
-- `stories_audience_gate` would then make it readable by the whole community, the audience widening D-716 forbids. A
-- member never UPDATES an item (the service never does), so that is refused outright, which also stops a re-point.
--
-- WHY THE INSERT GATES CARRY THE `social` TERM AND UPDATE/DELETE DO NOT (assumption A11): every insert gate of Phase 10
-- reads `social` from SQL; the service already stops an update or delete while `social` is off, and a social term on a
-- delete would only stop a creator from taking down their own highlight. A NULL role claim makes every branch null, which
-- DENIES (fail closed).
--
-- WR-04: the staff branch of `feed_posts_social_insert_gate` admitted any `'tenant'` post, so an admin_tenant or system
-- lane could insert one into a MEMBER community (the service refuses it, `resolveCommunityTarget`, but the database did not).
-- It now admits it only with no community or in an ORGANIZATION community of the caller's tenant.
--
-- WR-05: see the second statement of the hand-written half.
--
-- EXPAND-ONLY: no table, column, constraint, index or row changes; it tightens only writes the API never makes.
-- ONE-TASK REVERT: drop the seven policies and the trigger plus its function, restore the previous ALTER POLICY text of
-- `feed_posts_social_insert_gate` (the one in `20261111144148_feed_community_audience.sql`) and re-apply the function
-- body of `20261111150352_story_media_gate.sql` with `create or replace`.

CREATE POLICY "stories_member_delete_gate" ON "stories" AS RESTRICTIVE FOR DELETE TO "authenticated" USING (app.tenant_role() <> 'member');--> statement-breakpoint
